{"step_index":922,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:55:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:55:07+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:55:19+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:55:07+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:55:19+08:00\nThe search for \"self decrypting html javascript eval cipher payload offline browser file protocol\" returned the following summary:\nA **self-decrypting HTML payload** running via the local `file://` protocol relies entirely on client-side execution. Because it operates completely offline without a backend server, it packages an encrypted data payload alongside a plain JavaScript bootstrap routine[1][2]. When loaded into a browser, the bootstrap script decrypts the payload in memory and injects or executes it[3].\n\n---\n\n### Core Mechanics\n\n1. **The Wrapper (HTML + JS):** A clean structural wrapper containing minimal bootstrap JavaScript[3].\n2. **The Ciphertext:** The core payload (HTML, JavaScript, or application code) encoded and encrypted using a symmetric cipher (e.g., AES-GCM) stored directly inside a `<script>` or `<template>` tag[2].\n3. **The Key / Password:** Can be hardcoded into the bootstrap script (for obfuscation/local-only defense) or prompted from the user via a password box at runtime[2].\n4. **The Execution (`eval` / DOM Injection):** Once decrypted in memory, the payload is dynamically written to the DOM or executed via `eval()` / `Function()` constructor execution blocks[3].\n\n---\n\n### Conceptual Code Architecture\n\nBelow is a proof-of-concept demonstrating how a standalone HTML file can use the modern browser **Web Crypto API** (`crypto.subtle`) and AES-GCM to self-decrypt and execute an encrypted payload offline, triggered locally via the `file://` protocol.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <title>Self-Decrypting Offline Container</title>\n    <style>\n        body { font-family: sans-serif; background: #121212; color: #e0e0e0; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100vh; margin: 0; }\n        #loader { text-align: center; }\n        input, button { padding: 10px; margin-to\n<truncated 4123 bytes>\nou cannot use external `fetch()` calls, external scripts (`<script src=\"...\">`), or local module imports (`import ... from ...`) relative to the file path in most modern browsers. **The file must remain entirely monolithic (self-contained)**, embedding all code, styles, and data inline.\n2. **Web Crypto API Requirements:** \n   The `window.crypto.subtle` library functions natively inside offline contexts (`file://`) across most modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari), meaning robust modern cryptography (AES-GCM, PBKDF2) is fully operational without requiring an HTTP/HTTPS web server context.\n3. **Content Security Policy (CSP) & `eval()`:** \n   If local HTML files are forced to parse raw strings via `eval()` or dynamic `Function` instantiations after runtime decryption, strict local browser configurations or enterprise policies might occasionally flag or block execution if a restrictive meta-CSP is applied. However, native single-file dynamic DOM writing (`element.innerHTML` or creating script elements dynamically via `document.createElement('script')`) usually bypasses static heuristic blocks because the malicious or sensitive source code is not exposed natively in the initial raw text layout of the document.\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH50NnA5jetEO2o7b8JYV9cTYnIT0JNPQgWwLbrwc6Hv3BN5Dk0rZus8apn52_N-HqGZNTaPGaFlyaxSBVyLWnNSKVawtlVYF9wgDpXzQ7uoXToU-nXvO3NmAkj4zvBViAgVdM5oi8Hy3bXPqo=)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG1WlwkIzmNg_1A686KtvA3jIAOjn67tHI08whonIBCVXPyC33lj0W0jIFVRQjpNjhavHNBX7XLUXKrG4daEUOVLPuUMULwSyUsfhLFxzzm7vuol77bDWWERQg1TyrTlQ==)\n[3] [html-code-generator.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHoWiwuhzxNCi-FzYJ1pCIUFdZPow1bJrcrUR3jyVOsNyv6m2qhoYeXQtZhmkhulK9iTlQpzXDsVjAW27H6S6ydgCeCVNZozalCBPnlAwHGgJy-b7aUJcKx7IumtJ34NpEO6su30mn3xfC-8epu-64eIBOfIw==)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
