{"step_index":939,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:59:03Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:59:03+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:59:07+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:59:03+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:59:07+08:00\nThe search for \"vercel .vercelignore static html exclude directory from deployment\" returned the following summary:\nTo exclude a specific directory (or static HTML files) from being deployed to Vercel, you can use a `.vercelignore` file[1]. It works similarly to a `.gitignore` file[1] and must be placed in the **root directory** of your project[1].\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n\n1. Create a file named `.vercelignore` in your project's root folder[1].\n2. Add the path of the directory or file you want to exclude[1].\n\n#### Example 1: Exclude a specific static directory\nIf you have a folder named `admin` or `drafts` containing static HTML files that you don't want to upload or serve, add its path:\n\n```text\n# Exclude a specific directory\nadmin/\ndrafts/\n```\n\n#### Example 2: Exclude specific static HTML files\nIf you want to exclude individual HTML files from the root or elsewhere:\n\n```text\n# Exclude a single HTML file\nprivate.html\nold-index.html\n```\n\n---\n\n### Alternative Approach: Allowlist Mode (Ignore Everything Else)\nIf your project contains a lot of source files and you only want to deploy a specific set of static HTML files or folders, you can invert the logic by ignoring everything (`/*`) and explicitly allowlisting what you need using `!`[1]:\n\n```text\n# 1. Ignore everything in the root\n/*\n\n# 2. Allow only specific directories/files you want deployed\n!index.html\n!about.html\n!assets/\n!css/\n!js/\n```\n\n### Important Notes:\n* **Git vs Vercel:** `.vercelignore` only prevents files from being uploaded to Vercel's deployment servers[1]. It does **not** affect your local Git repository or git commits.\n* **Build Optimization:** Excluding unused static directories and heavy files helps make your deployment process faster[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG98A7rp24aqnVCJ1U8bbSwlWj0gXzymDNCiHXcE7P3BHXwmUkwsCS_xPo2INEhPcWotq9LVKb8MPl0R0aE3Ks7uwZFETSe44TrD_71_1qFxmGdmeHt05xndU3L30WcyBdHUrbXV1yv)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
