unctionality; key parameters include `renameGlobals: false`, `selfDefending: false`, and `debugProtection: false` to ensure inline script and browser compatibility. Additionally, string splitting and shuffling are enabled to further guard against reverse engineering.\n\n\nThe analysis now considers advanced obfuscation options. Investigating whether chained string array wrappers and object key transformations enhance resistance. Evaluating the inclusion of a second encryption layer for the already obfuscated JavaScript, weighing the benefits against potential complexities. Carefully considering whether combining the `javascript-obfuscator` with encryption inside a `<script>` offers superior protection.\n\n\nThe application's logic is fully encrypted within a script tag, employing RC4 decryption performed by an obfuscated loader script. This loader dynamically executes the decrypted code using `new Function()`. Crucially, verifying that event handlers and global functions in both HTML files remain functional after decryption is essential.\n\n\nNo inline event handlers (`onclick`, `onload`, etc.) are present in the HTML; all event bindings occur within JavaScript. Confirmed this with file-system regex checks on both HTML files. Additionally, the `<script>` tag within the obfuscated script utilizes Base64 encoding; the nature of Base64 prevents premature closure of the tag. Verified that Content Security Policy (CSP) is not restrictively configured, and `new Function(...)` is allowed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"node -e \\\"\\nconst fs = require('fs');\\n['index.html', 'teacher.html'].forEach(f => {\\n  const html = fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8').replace(/<script[\\\\s\\\\S]*?<\\\\/script>/gi, '');\\n  const m = html.match(/\\\\son\\\\w+\\\\s*=/gi);\\n  console.log(f, 'inline on* attributes:', m || 'NONE');\\n  const meta = html.match(/<meta[^>]*>/gi);\\n  console.log(f, 'meta tags:', meta);\\n});\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Check inline HTML event handlers and meta tags\""}}]}
