{"step_index":942,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:59:25Z","input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_tokens":368420,"output_tokens":189,"thinking":"Initial assessment: project uses `package.json`, suggesting an npm-based deployment. Suspecting potential conflict during the deployment process, looking into build configurations. Considering if any tooling present in `package.json` might be causing issues.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"vercel package.json present without build script static html vercelignore\""}}]}
{"step_index":943,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:59:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:59:31+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:59:35+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:59:31+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:59:35+08:00\nThe search for \"vercel package.json present without build script static html vercelignore\" returned the following summary:\nWhen deploying a **static HTML site** to Vercel that includes a `package.json` file (even though it doesn't require a build script), Vercel might accidentally try to look for a build script or misinterpret how to deploy it. \n\nTo ensure Vercel deploys your raw static HTML files correctly without throwing errors about a missing build script, follow these configuration steps:\n\n### 1. Tell Vercel Not to Run a Build Command\nBecause your site is pure HTML/CSS/JS and doesn’t need compilation, you must override Vercel's default build behaviors[1]:\n\n* **Via the Vercel Dashboard:**\n  1. Go to your project dashboard on Vercel[2].\n  2. Navigate to **Settings** > **Build & Development Settings**[2].\n  3. Set the **Framework Preset** to **Other**[1].\n  4. Enable the **Override** toggle next to the **Build Command** and leave the text input completely **empty**[1].\n  5. (Optional) If your HTML files are sitting in a specific folder like `public` or `dist`, specify that as the **Output Directory**. If they are in the root directory, you can leave it blank or set it to `./`.\n  6. Click **Save**[1] and trigger a **Redeploy**[2].\n\n* **Via a `vercel.json` file (Alternative):**\n  Create a `vercel.json` file in the root of your project to explicitly command Vercel to skip building[3]:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"framework\": null,\n    \"buildCommand\": \"\",\n    \"outputDirectory\": \".\"\n  }\n  ```\n  *(Note: If your static files live inside a folder like `public`, change `\"outputDirectory\": \"public\"`)*.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Configure `.vercelignore` (If Needed)\nIf you have utility scripts, markdown files, node modules, or config files in your repository that you **do not** want uploaded or exposed on your live static site, use a `.vercelignore` file[4].\n\nCreate a `.vercelignore` file in your root directory[4]. It functions similarly to a `.gitignore` file[4]:\n\n```text\n# Ignore local development and dependency files\nnode_modules/\npackage-lock.json\nyarn.lock\npnpm-lock.yaml\n\n# Ignore documentation or local markdown files\nREADME.md\n.git/\n.gitignore\n```\n\nIf you want to whitelist *only* your static assets and ignore everything else by default, you can use the strict root-ignore pattern[4]:\n```text\n# Ignore everything on root first\n/*\n\n# Then explicitly allow only what is needed for the static site\n!index.html\n!about.html\n!/assets\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG3Sdk8g0jtdDvyZXLdEWB1XA35_EeWNaJaXe_LFowqBC7ZYKF1i7tO8nRyzzDxPbDxsatN0EOY6BN-afM3gN5EfelaYl28mMZ92mpZRbw_1gpDB7ioidXAitfkOKeF8IC-yL7MWDc=)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHYaUoJE133OAHeH59K3Tv9a6gCbtnOa_FycRIgilckEXDV_UQj0OLVLMsl5HGe3SxgCXRFs5mXzhc35O_CD495y2WortNjI2s_JrfPik_hpQgypvXR62qefufF9WcT8zziGBcg1LkDLSsQKtRUvq-KHbLrCKxMlAt09m21UfRLUKxCrn95FIKhWxVlzYWVmjoesGZU5411cMAFGrnef5-cctr0ih0=)\n[3] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEqiv_X5tKWEUtzGfyyrr27CYQ8SKzB8QAKCXkfHmi3YwG_GqL0ZB6C0s9IrE6Oh79OwLWRFGj74W0vbEA4Sz7vzQkBZ9nX6l6zyx63fgQIDpYSOm4hJMhLLqSaL3cniRZ1dt6GH4Y0DHlJBLQilQA=)\n[4] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE7qr9djvn7LqogXhxfuSo0kMi_3ThUQ0hyqQrhkJgTJcsBj55Ja0F0K53DRtP6g4ODXQwJCfOwcmW5QkKGeg55pWGLIja57zvisQWC1NbckqSWDVveaETshLlSYo5lqX4aQX1u0eGF)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":944,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:59:35Z","input_tokens":3516,"cache_read_tokens":368618,"output_tokens":3993,"thinking":"The search result highlighted a crucial `.vercelignore` configuration. Excluding `package.json` in allowlist mode appears essential, given its potential impact on deployment. This suggests the deployment failure might stem from the `package.json` file being inadvertently included or excluded from the deployment, and this configuration needs careful testing to verify the root cause.\n\n\nConsidering that the primary goal is a static HTML deployment, the ideal `.vercelignore` configuration aims for the root to remain completely static. This involves isolating build dependencies within a subdirectory (`raw/`) to ensure no attempt is made to install `node_modules` at the project's root. The subdirectory strategy allows clean separation of the raw, editable source files from the deployment files.\n\n\nThe `.vercelignore` configuration effectively blocks specified files and directories, ensuring they are not uploaded or publicly accessible on Vercel. This behavior extends to both Git-linked and Vercel CLI deployments. The proposed obfuscation plan is likely a critical next step to verify.\n\n\nWith Stage 1 obfuscation alone, the resulting HTML contains a single large, obviously obfuscated JavaScript block. Adding Stage 2 creates an \"encrypted shell,\" placing the core logic within a `<script>` with a cipher, loaded by a smaller, obfuscated bootstrap script. Comparing these two configurations is critical to verify the effect of each stage.\n\n\nThe obfuscation achieves a layered defense: initial upload to AI models yields only obfuscated script tags and a small RC4 loader. Stage 2, even when decoded, reveals only Stage 1's already obfuscated code, providing a multi-stage deterrent. Performance analysis shows the JavaScript decryption, even on mobile, is negligibly fast, adding minimal overhead.\n\nCompatibility is now the focus: investigating if the raw HTML files rely on global variables or functions, and if the two stages work seamlessly together. Inline HTML attributes were checked earlier with negative results, so now to focus on external resources.\n\n\nInitial investigation reveals no reliance on global variables or functions outside the single app `<script>` block on each page. Specifically, the code inside `raw/index.html` uses `document.getElementById('local-db-vault')` to access content, and does not depend on `window.` global namespace. The code within the `new Function(decoded)` scope, including function declarations and `const`/`let` declarations, is locally scoped. The `<script>` tag's placement at the end of the `<body>` ensures DOM elements are fully loaded before script execution.\n\n\nAll synchronous calls within `index.html` and `teacher.html` execute without timing issues or missing DOM elements. CSS styling and HTML structure remain identical after modifications, specifically the visual layout and button IDs, including the bullet points.\n\nNext, verifying compliance with specific project rules. Planning a comprehensive implementation with an `implementation_plan.md` artifact is the next logical step.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan to preserve raw un-obfuscated source copies in raw/, build double-layered AST-obfuscated and cipher-sealed index.html and teacher.html, prevent raw/ exposure on Vercel via .vercelignore, update injectVault to target #local-db-vault cleanly, and verify live functionality across Edge/Node/Firestore.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan: Double-Layer Obfuscation & Encrypted Runtime with Raw Source Copies\\n\\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\\n1. **Preserve Raw Editable Source Copies (`raw/`):**\\n   - Save un-obfuscated, clean source copies at `raw/index.html` and `raw/teacher.html` (maintaining 100% of current functionality and zero in-code comments per Rule 9).\\n   - Store local build tooling strictly inside `raw/` (`raw/package.json`, `raw/build.cjs`) so the project root remains clean static HTML/JSON without polluting root with `node_modules/`.\\n2. **Generate Double-Layer Hardened Production Files ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) & [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)):**\\n   - **Stage 1 (AST Obfuscation via `javascript-obfuscator`):** Compiles the application `<script>` with `controlFlowFlattening` (`0.75`), `deadCodeInjection` (`0.35`), `numbersToExpressions: true`, `splitStrings` (chunk length `5`), `stringArrayEncoding: ['rc4']` with rotation/wrappers, `transformObjectKeys: true`, `identifierNamesGenerator: 'hexadecimal'`, `compact: true`, and `selfDefending: false` / `debugProtection: false` (explicitly disabled per verified inline-HTML research to prevent parser whitespace infinite loops and mobile browser freezes).\\n   - **Stage 2 (Encrypted Self-Unpacking Runtime Shell):** Encrypts the entire Stage-1 obfuscated JS payload into `<script id=\\\"local-runtime-cipher\\\" type=\\\"application/octet-stream\\\">` using a pure-JS KSA+PRGA stream cipher + split/permuted key fragments, paired with a compact loader `<script>` that is itself AST-obfuscated (`rc4` strings, `numbersToExpressions`, hexadecimal names) and executes the unpacked script synchronously in memory (`new Function(...)()`). Works offline on `file:///` and HTTPS without Web Crypto Secure Context restrictions.\\n3. **Resilient Embedded Vault Slot (`#local-db-vault`):**\\n   - Decouple the embedded encrypted quiz slot in `raw/index.html` into `<script id=\\\"local-db-vault\\\" type=\\\"application/octet-s\n<truncated 5433 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
